# Docker build-context filter for the engine containers whose image_build_context is the repo root
# (currently containers/recovery — see apps/recovery-worker/wrangler.jsonc). A .dockerignore is read
# from the build-context root, so an engine container that builds on the crates/ workspace needs this
# file HERE, not beside its Dockerfile. Allowlist only the source the engine images copy — the Rust
# workspace and the container hosts — so .git, secrets (.dev.vars), node_modules, and every package's
# build output never transit to the builder. Each Dockerfile still COPYs only its own subset.
*
!crates
!containers
# Never ship build output even from the allowlisted trees.
**/target
**/node_modules
